[TEXT] **Root cause found.** The nftables FORWARD chain on **router6** has explicit DROP rules:

```
iifname "eth2" meta l4proto tcp  → DROP  (all TCP entering from eth2)
iifname "eth2" meta l4proto udp  → DROP  (all UDP entering from eth2)
iifname "eth2"                   → DROP  (all other traffic entering from eth2) ← 59 pkts/5072B already counted
```

eth2 is the **r6_r3 backbone link**. Every packet arriving from the backbone (router3/router2/router1/router0 side) and destined for the 172.18.51.x or 172.18.50.x hosts is dropped in the FORWARD chain. The only exception is TCP port 80 from 172.16.10.0/24 to 172.18.51.1. ip_forward is 1, so the issue is purely the ACL. And router3 can ping router6.eth2 (10.50.1.2) with 0% loss — the link itself is fine.

